{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/85834-why-take-a-glitch-for-compromises","id":85834,"title":"Why take a Glitch for Compromises?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-06T21:52:51-08:00","id":85834,"title":"Why take a Glitch for Compromises?","content":"So, in the results presented for Compromise rolls (except for Exceptional Success), the player gets to choose between taking a Condition (which leads to story, and the resolution of it gives a beat) or rolling for a Glitch (temporary or permanent, depending, but neither of which is a beat generator). So far none of my players have gone for the glitch when Conditions drive character advancement.<br /> <br /> Is there ever a reason for them to take the glitch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/72-vassilyomega","name":"VassilyOmega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar72_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T22:03:59-08:00","id":85835,"title":"","content":"When taking one of the Conditions would lead to very bad things for the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:20:50-08:00","id":86059,"title":"","content":"My players were about 50/50. Sure, taking a Condition gives you a Beat, but sometimes they just couldn't find or think of one that fit the situation, and sometimes gaining a glitch just seemed like the right choice, narratively. <br /> <br /> I'd advocate treating a glitch like a Flaw - if it inconveniences you in play, you get a Beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T11:10:59-08:00","id":86127,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestion, blackhatmatt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/72-vassilyomega","name":"VassilyOmega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar72_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T13:00:16-08:00","id":86202,"title":"","content":"If I'm not mistaken the 3 conditions you get for compromise rolls in human form: Spooked, Shaken, and Guilty, don't give beats for resolving, do they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2460-tazar-yoot","name":"Tazar Yoot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T13:33:05-08:00","id":86222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tazar Yoot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/85834-why-take-a-glitch-for-compromises?p=86202#post86202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not mistaken the 3 conditions you get for compromise rolls in human form: Spooked, Shaken, and Guilty, don't give beats for resolving, do they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Spooked and Shaken do absolutely nothing mechanically aside from incentivize resolving them to get Beats, this would be a rather nonsensical exception to the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T13:50:09-08:00","id":86233,"title":"","content":"So are you saying beats should be awarded for those 3 conditions? The reason I ask is because under those conditions descriptions for the Beat section is says n/a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2460-tazar-yoot","name":"Tazar Yoot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T13:51:51-08:00","id":86234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tazar Yoot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/85834-why-take-a-glitch-for-compromises?p=86233#post86233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are you saying beats should be awarded for those 3 conditions? The reason I ask is because under those conditions descriptions for the Beat section is says n/a.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the &quot;Beat&quot; section is for getting Beats <i>without</i> resolving the Condition. That's how Persistent Conditions work, and none of those three are Persistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}